{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"The round 4 change fixes R3-N1’s negated marker case. The focused tests pass, and the checkout remains clean. I’m treating the remaining marker grammar gap as one blocker because the parser does not enforce the required assumption-plus-reason form. I’ll submit the full round-aware draft to the dispatched engine now."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"export POSE_REVIEW_CLI=/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-ready\ncat <<'POSE_DRAFT_INPUT' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\nN1 is a medium blocker at [accepted_limits.go:31](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1298900130/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:31). The matcher allows “Accepted because …” at the start of an entry, so a limit can omit the required assumption (for example, “Accepted because this is low risk”). It also captures through the end of the line and counts words in later text as the reason (for example, “Assumption. Accepted because. Unrelated later details.”). Both can pass ready-check without the required assumption-and-reason form. The focused Go tests passed: go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run '\"'AcceptedLimit|WithinASealedLimit|ReadyCheckJudges|Brief|Conclud'. Required validation commands could not compile because the read-only sandbox blocks Go build/cache writes; sealed build and unit evidence is cited below.\n\n| Criterion | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| assumption-integrity | failed (N1) | N1; pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:31 |\n| backend-concurrency | passed | unit:pose-mcp/go/test |\n| backend-contracts | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration |\n| backend-input-errors | failed (N1) | N1 |\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence |\n| backend-observability | passed | unit:pose-mcp/go/test |\n| compatibility | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration |\n| correctness | failed (N1) | N1 |\n| design-causality | passed | structure:design-bd1cd2f1473c8787 |\n| documentation | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration |\n| operability | failed (N1) | N1 |\n| requirements | failed (N1) | N1 |\n| scope | passed | structure:design-bd1cd2f1473c8787 |\n| security | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration |\n| solution-proportionality | passed | structure:design-bd1cd2f1473c8787 |\n\nR3-N1 is fixed: the new sentence-opening rule rejects “Not accepted because …”, and the focused tests pass. I swept all 18 changed paths and rechecked the parser and ready-check, ADR matching, qualified composite IDs, plan/bundle fields and digests, brief v11, conclusion conversion and blockers, closeout, manuals and scaffold parity, and L1/L2. The conclusion gate rejects unsealed limit IDs and missing rationales; D1 leaves semantic membership to reviewer judgment. L1 discloses author-controlled breadth and requires disputes to block; L2 is digest-bound and requires a new bundle after edits, so both are justified.\n\n\"'```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\n      \"line\": 31,\n      \"summary\": \"The accepted-limit reason matcher permits the marker at entry start without a preceding assumption, and its greedy capture counts later sentence text as the reason. Reason-only entries and entries with an empty reason followed by unrelated prose therefore pass ready-check, contrary to R1/R4.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits_test.go:106\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed all 18 paths in the subject and the round 4 parser/test delta. Traced accepted-limit parsing and lint diagnostics, ADR coverage, qualified IDs across composite scopes, plan/bundle serialization and digests, brief v11, finding-to-attestation conversion, within-limit blockers, closeout, docs and scaffold parity. Checked R3-N1, the L1/L2 justifications, and the focused accepted-limit, brief and conclusion tests.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified that limits are qualified in composite scopes and sealed into the plan and bundle. L2'\"'s edit-after-seal boundary is bound by the digest; L1's author-controlled breadth is disclosed and disputable. The parser still permits an entry without a preceding assumption or an immediate reason (N1).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The parser and conclusion changes add immutable review data without shared mutable state, asynchronous work or a new cancellation/lifecycle path. The sealed pose-mcp unit suite passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The v11 brief and attestation carry the sealed limit and finding attribution; optional plan and bundle fields are omitted when empty. The sealed integration contract test passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Plan, bundle, brief and attestation consumers remain connected in the review flow. The integration assessment reported unobserved HTTP consumers for /admin/refresh, /healthz and /mcp, outside the changed review-limit paths; the sealed bundle-convergence test passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Parser failures return an accepted-limit diagnostic, and the conclusion gate names unsealed IDs or missing rationales. The sealed unit suite passes; N1 is a validation false pass.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The review brief advances to v11, while optional fields are omitted when empty to preserve prior plan and bundle digests. Reviewed the version/digest tests and the sealed template immutability integration.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-bd1cd2f1473c8787\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1 parses and seals limits, R2 renders them in brief v11, R3 records the within-limit disposition, and R4 checks reasons and ADR references. D1 delegates semantic scope classification to the reviewer and requires a sealed ID plus rationale; D2 binds limits into the plan digest and omits empty values. The sealed design assessment reports no structural deltas.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed the English and Portuguese manuals and scaffold copies against runtime behavior. They describe brief v11, sealed limits and qualified composite IDs consistently; the sealed template parity integration passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-bd1cd2f1473c8787\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation remains within accepted-limit parsing, plan/bundle sealing, brief rendering, finding attribution and readiness lint behavior named by the spec. The sealed design assessment reports no structural deltas.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The conclusion gate requires an ID sealed in the bundle and a rationale; an unsealed ID blocks approval. D1 leaves semantic membership to reviewer judgment and the brief exposes each declared limit. No new path or authority input is introduced.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-bd1cd2f1473c8787\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A shared parser is the smallest sufficient path through readiness, planning and the review brief; optional fields preserve empty-plan and bundle digests. Separate parsers or a speculative threat taxonomy add cost without serving R1–R4. The marker matcher should enforce the declared assumption-plus-reason grammar. This design would need reconsideration if semantic membership had to be machine-proven rather than reviewer-judged.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran through the dispatched engine and exited 0. It selected cs-a557ed8434d4/head 6c5a896e2a77d14eb1e42bc703591936866948df rather than this brief's cs-966e310459b2/head 3c6f7b9c6bbb1c935bf3b8a1ad68f245693480f0, and emitted repository-wide orphan warnings; this is a successful invocation, not scoped proof.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-bd1cd2f1473c8787\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The sealed design evidence passes with no structural deltas. The ad hoc assessment also saw 18 paths and no deltas, though its reported subject head differed from this brief.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the recommended pose-mcp discovery assessment; it completed and discovered the component.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the integration assessment. Its three unobserved HTTP consumer references are outside the changed review-limit paths; the relevant sealed bundle-convergence integration passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The repository-wide scan was incomplete because two unrelated specs could not be read and it reported one uncovered debt item. It identified no issue in the changed subject.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Deferred because this check requires the review conclusion; this run must not record an attestation.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Deferred because this check requires the review conclusion; this run must not record an attestation.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the recommended component review suggestion; it selected backend, security and documentation review areas.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The strict surface check passed with zero findings; the sealed lint-spec integration covers the readiness surface.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the required command; the read-only sandbox blocked Go build/cache writes before validation could complete. The sealed build evidence passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the required module command; the read-only sandbox blocked Go build/cache writes before validation could complete. Sealed unit evidence passes, and the focused accepted-limit/brief/conclusion tests passed in this run.\\\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\"'```\nPOSE_DRAFT_INPUT'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
