dle-convergence test passes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Parser failures return an accepted-limit diagnostic, and the conclusion gate names unsealed IDs or missing rationales. The sealed unit suite passes; N1 is a validation false pass.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The review brief advances to v11, while optional fields are omitted when empty to preserve prior plan and bundle digests. Reviewed the version/digest tests and the sealed template immutability integration.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-bd1cd2f1473c8787\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1 parses and seals limits, R2 renders them in brief v11, R3 records the within-limit disposition, and R4 checks reasons and ADR references. D1 delegates semantic scope classification to the reviewer and requires a sealed ID plus rationale; D2 binds limits into the plan digest and omits empty values. The sealed design assessment reports no structural deltas.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed the English and Portuguese manuals and scaffold copies against runtime behavior. They describe brief v11, sealed limits and qualified composite IDs consistently;