{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nN1 is a medium blocker at [accepted_limits.go:31](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1298900130/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:31). The matcher allows “Accepted because …” at the start of an entry, so a limit can omit the required assumption (for example, “Accepted because this is low risk”). It also captures through the end of the line and counts words in later text as the reason (for example, “Assumption. Accepted because. Unrelated later details.”). Both can pass ready-check without the required assumption-and-reason form. The focused Go tests passed: `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'AcceptedLimit|WithinASealedLimit|ReadyCheckJudges|Brief|Conclud'`. Required validation commands could not compile because the read-only sandbox blocks Go build/cache writes; sealed build and unit evidence is cited below.\n\n| Criterion | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| assumption-integrity | failed (N1) | N1; pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:31 |\n| backend-concurrency | passed | unit:pose-mcp/go/test |\n| backend-contracts | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration |\n| backend-input-errors | failed (N1) | N1 |\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence |\n| backend-observability | passed | unit:pose-mcp/go/test |\n| compatibility | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration |\n| correctness | failed (N1) | N1 |\n| design-causality | passed | structure:design-bd1cd2f1473c8787 |\n| documentation | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration |\n| operability | failed (N1) | N1 |\n| requirements | failed (N1) | N1 |\n| scope | passed | structure:design-bd1cd2f1473c8787 |\n| security | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration |